From 3e8bfb5fa563ee032b724ebb40928cefdd8a45b6 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Anton Palgunov <toxblh@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 9 Sep 2026 02:26:44 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] gdk: add an iOS backend (UIKit, cairo only)

A minimal GDK backend for iOS: UIKit owns the main thread, GTK runs
on its own thread and hops to the main queue for UIKit work. Each
GdkSurface is a UIView; toplevels fill the root view, popups are
subviews positioned by the popup layout helper. Drawing goes through
a cairo image buffer that becomes the layer's CGImage each frame.
Touches become GDK touch events (the first finger emulates the
pointer); a GDK grab redirects hit testing to the grabbed view so
autohide popups close on outside taps. No GL, no clipboard, no
on-screen keyboard yet.

The macOS-only pieces (SDK version check, quartz color picker) are
now gated on the macOS backend instead of __APPLE__.
